# Templates

`.rocci` templates are HTML for Roc: `@component`, `@css`,
markup, and directives. A PascalCase component lowers to a pure Roc `Html`
function.

Stop here if you only preview components into an existing `main.roc`. You do
not need the Applications layer until you want generated dispatch or you
own routing yourself.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/components/", title: "Components", summary: "Declare, call, and preview. Cataloged styling example."]
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/markup/", title: "Markup", summary: "Tags, attributes, interpolations, scoped CSS, stable ids."]
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/directives/", title: "Directives", summary: "@if, @for, @match, @let."]
:card-grid.end

Exact forms: [language reference](/docs/reference/language/).
When you need HTTP: [Applications](/docs/applications/).
